#* {{quote-text|en|year=2006|author=Andrew Sneddon|title=Action and Responsibility|page=145|passage=In a variety of places, O'Shaughnessy argues that there is an internal relation between trying and the events that '''tryings''' produce. For example, he argues that tryings are not independently specifiable except as would-be causes of physical events.}}
